\q1 \v 16 \rb Nations|גוֹיִם֙\rb* \rb will see|יִרְא֤וּ\rb* \rb and be ashamed,|וְיֵבֹ֔שׁוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb deprived of all|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb their might.|גְּבֽוּרָתָ֑ם\rb*
\q1 \rb They will put|יָשִׂ֤ימוּ\rb* \rb their hands|יָד֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb their mouths,|פֶּ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and their ears|אָזְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb will become deaf.|תֶּחֱרַֽשְׁנָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb They will lick|יְלַחֲכ֤וּ\rb* \rb the dust|עָפָר֙\rb* \rb like a snake,|כַּנָּחָ֔שׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb like reptiles slithering|כְּזֹחֲלֵ֣י\rb* \rb on the ground.|אֶ֔רֶץ\rb*
\q1 \rb They will come trembling|יִרְגְּז֖וּ\rb* \rb from their strongholds|מִמִּסְגְּרֹֽתֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb in the presence of|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb our God;|אֱלֹהֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb they will tremble|יִפְחָ֔דוּ\rb* \rb in fear|וְיִֽרְא֖וּ\rb* \rb of You.|מִמֶּֽךָּ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 18 \rb Who|מִי־\rb* \rb is a God|אֵ֣ל\rb* \rb like You,|כָּמ֗וֹךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb who pardons|נֹשֵׂ֤א\rb* \rb iniquity|עָוֺן֙\rb*
\q1 \rb and passes|וְעֹבֵ֣ר\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the transgression|פֶּ֔שַׁע\rb*
\q2 \rb of the remnant|לִשְׁאֵרִ֖ית\rb* \rb of His inheritance—|נַחֲלָת֑וֹ\rb*
\q1 \rb who does not|לֹא־\rb* \rb retain|הֶחֱזִ֤יק\rb* \rb His anger|אַפּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb forever,|לָעַד֙\rb*
\q2 \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb He|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb delights|חָפֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb in loving devotion?|חֶ֖סֶד\rb*\f + \fr 7:18 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa chesed \ft are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as \fqa loving devotion\ft ; the range of meaning includes \fqa love\ft , \fqa goodness\ft , \fqa kindness\ft , \fqa faithfulness\ft , and \fqa mercy\ft , as well as \fqa loyalty to a covenant\ft .\f*
\q1 \v 19 \rb He will again|יָשׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb have compassion on us;|יְרַֽחֲמֵ֔נוּ\rb*
